== Broomsticks | Q1: Trade (C1.1)

A small country has demand $P = 16 - Q_d/4$ and supply $P = 4 + Q_s/4$. Its no-trade equilibrium price is 10 coins. The world price is 6 coins. Assume competitive markets and no externalities.

a) At the world price, calculate $Q_d$, $Q_s$, and trade volume. Does the country import or export?
#v(0.65in)
b) Compared with no trade, do domestic buyers gain or lose? Sellers? Does domestic total surplus rise or fall?
#v(0.35in)

== Q2: Tariff (C1.2)

The country imposes a tariff of 2 coins per imported broomstick. Imports continue.

a) Calculate the domestic price, $Q_d$, $Q_s$, imports, and tariff revenue.
#v(0.65in)
b) Compared with free trade, do domestic buyers gain or lose? Sellers?
#v(0.25in)
c) On the supplied demand and supply graph, mark the free-trade and tariff prices, and shade the two DWL regions. You do not need to calculate their areas.
